@startuml
!include ../../common/eztrade-style.puml

title EZTrade Sequence - JWT Login and Session Restoration
autonumber

actor "User" as User
participant "LoginPage" as LoginPage
participant "AuthProvider\nuseAuth()" as AuthProvider
participant "authApi" as AuthApi
participant "AuthController\nPOST /auth/login" as AuthController
participant "AuthService" as AuthService
participant "AuthenticationProvider" as AuthProviderBackend
participant "JwtService" as JwtService
database "localStorage" as LocalStorage
participant "UserController\nGET /api/user" as UserController
participant "UserService / repository" as UserService

User -> LoginPage : sends identifier + password
LoginPage -> AuthProvider : login(identifier, password)
AuthProvider -> AuthApi : login(...)
AuthApi -> AuthController : POST /auth/login\n{ email, password }
AuthController -> AuthService : login(identifier, password)
AuthService -> AuthProviderBackend : authenticate credentials
AuthProviderBackend --> AuthService : authenticated principal
AuthService -> JwtService : generateToken(...)
JwtService --> AuthService : JWT
AuthService --> AuthController : token
AuthController --> AuthApi : 200 JwtResponse
AuthApi --> AuthProvider : token
AuthProvider -> AuthProvider : decodes JWT payload\nclient-side only
AuthProvider -> LocalStorage : set token
AuthProvider -> AuthApi : getUser(payload.sub,\nwith token)
AuthApi -> UserController : GET /api/user?email=...
UserController -> UserService : getUser(email)
UserService --> UserController : User domain model
UserController --> AuthApi : UserDTO
AuthApi --> AuthProvider : UserProfile
AuthProvider -> LocalStorage : set user
AuthProvider --> LoginPage : session ready
LoginPage -> User : router.push("/")

note bottom
Evidence: frontend/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx, lib/auth-context.tsx,
features/auth/api.ts, AuthController.java, AuthService.java, and JwtService.java.
The frontend decodes the JWT only for UX/session restoration; signature validation is the backend's responsibility.
end note

@enduml
